@startuml
title stm — ButtonTestRunner lifecycle
[*] --> ReleaseWait
ReleaseWait --> Ready : all buttons released for 30 ms
Ready --> ReleaseWait : multiple-button selection / reject
Ready --> Running : single press stable 30 ms / start selected scenario
Running --> Fault : initialization, submission, completion or cleanup error
Running --> ReleaseWait : final TX_SUCCESS or stop / cleanup succeeds
Ready --> ReleaseWait : USB stop
Fault --> Fault : button press or USB stop / no re-arm
state Running {
  [*] --> Waiting
  Waiting --> Pending : due / submit single-shot
  Pending --> Waiting : TX_SUCCESS and more attempts remain
}
note right of Running
First attempt +1000 ms, then at most 1 Hz.
Busy button presses are discarded, never queued.
USB loss does not change this state.
end note
note right of Fault
Inspect bench and reset MCU.
Reset returns to ReleaseWait, not emission.
Cleanup may be retried by USB stop,
but does not clear the runner fault latch.
end note
@enduml
